    "result_text": "The implementation is complete and verified. `BUILD SUCCESS`, and the acceptance test (`Tests run: 1, Failures: 0, Errors: 0`) passes.\n\n## What I changed\n\n**Consolidated duplicate detection into one derived `identityKey`** = `normalizedTelephone + '|' + (email or empty) + '|' + householdId`:\n\n- **`IdentityKey.java`** (new) \u2014 derives the key for any `Owner`: telephone normalized to E.164 (falling back to the raw value if it can't form a valid number, so the key is always defined), email lower-cased or empty, householdId or empty.\n- **`EnsureUniqueIdentity.java`** (new) \u2014 the single check. Rejects with 409 (`DuplicateIdentityException`) only when the new owner's **whole** identityKey equals an existing owner's. It runs **after** `AssignHousehold` so the new owner's `householdId` is finalized before its key is derived.\n- **`DuplicateIdentityException` + handler + escalation YAML** (new) \u2014 respond 409 with a `ProblemDetail`, mirroring the existing escalation pattern.\n- **`owners.POST.yml`** \u2014 removed the three separate `ensureUniqueTelephone` / `ensureUniqueEmail` / `ensureUniqueHousehold` steps and wired in `ensureUniqueIdentity` after `assignHousehold`.\n- **`openapi.yml` + `OwnerMapper`** \u2014 added the read-only `identityKey` field to the `Owner` schema and populate it via a MapStruct expression, so it is **returned** on every owner response.\n- **Deleted** the three superseded `EnsureUnique*` functions and their `Duplicate{Telephone,Email,Household}` exceptions/handlers/escalation YAMLs, and updated two stale javadoc `@link`s.\n\n### Behaviour change (as specified)\nBecause telephone is part of the key, two members of the same household (same `householdId`) with **different** telephones now have different identityKeys and are **both allowed** \u2014 only an exact full-key match is a duplicate. The acceptance test confirms the collision case: a second owner reusing the first's telephone (same empty email, same empty householdId) yields an identical `identityKey` and is rejected with 409.",
